==Indonesian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|id|ms|itu}}, from {{inh|id|poz-mly-pro|*(i)tu(ʔ)}}, from {{inh|id|poz-pro|*(i-)tu}}, from {{inh|id|map-pro|*(i-)Cu}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{id-pr}}

===Determiner===
{{head|id|determiner}}

# [[that]] {{gloss|what is being indicated}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|id|pronoun}}

# [[it]] {{gloss|that thing}}

===Verb===
{{head|id|verb}}

# {{lb|id|copulative}} to [[be]]
#: {{ux|id|Apa '''itu''' bahasa?|What '''is''' language?}}
#: {{ux|id|Tuhan '''itu''' nyata.|God '''is''' real.}}
#: {{ux|id|Dia '''itu''' seorang pekerja keras.|He '''is''' a hard worker.}}

====Usage notes====
Together with {{m|id|ini}}, these can be placed following (in the standard language) or preceding the noun, the latter possibly due to the influence of {{w|Malay trade and creole languages}} of eastern Indonesia.

